# The repo is PUBLIC. This folder is an allowlist: the engine's code, its tests and the shipped voice
# clips go in; everything a call, a customer, a key or the sales work produces stays on the server.
# Kept out on purpose (untracked, in the checkout's backend/voice; deploy.sh links each one into every
# release, so it survives deploys):
#   .env (every key), service.env (the database the service uses), .venv/
#   calls/ turns.jsonl (real calls and transcripts), suppressed.jsonl (people who asked not to be called),
#   cache/ (voice clips made at runtime), prompt.md (the sales prompt of Aixel Labs' own line)
#   and local notes: HANDOFF.md (account ids), research/, demo/, one-off scripts.
#   tests/sim/ tests/linecache/: generated test transcripts and audio.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/*.py
!/requirements.txt
!/index.html
!/fillers/
!/tests/
/tests/*
!/tests/*.py
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# one-offs: the move off the voicelab tunnel; the 9 -> 6 voice collections (2026-10-21); provider keys (2026-10-22). Delete once done.
/repoint_numbers.py
/migrate_voice_accounts.py
/migrate_voice_keys.py
